# Rank 1789 / CVE-2025-61600: the IMAP/ManageSieve command receiver
# parsed quoted arguments one byte at a time, and every arm of the
# quoted-argument state that appends to the accumulator carried the
# 4096-byte bound except the escaped-backslash arm -- `b'\\' => { if
# escaped { self.buf.push(ch); } ... }` pushed with no comparison at
# all, so a peer sending a quoted argument made of escaped
# backslashes grew the buffer past the cap without limit
# (unbounded per-connection accumulation, CWE-400; fix commit
# a8e631e88 "IMAP: Check buf size before pushing escape sequences
# within quoted literals"). The fixed revision wraps that one push in the same
# `self.buf.len() < QUOTED_ARG_MAX_LEN` test its sibling arms
# carry, lifting the literal into a named constant; the
# sibling arms' bounds and the rest of the state machine are
# unchanged, which is what makes the defect an arm-local omission
# rather than a missing global cap.
#
# ATTENTION, rechecked: branch regions inside a Rust loop. The
# discriminating fact is per-arm -- "this append is dominated by a
# size comparison" -- and the engine has the machinery for exactly
# that relation (`unless X.dominates coveredBy <check>` over the
# structured control regions). It is unusable here because the Rust
# frontend lowers no loop: `rsConv.stmtH` carries cases for
# statement-position `if_expression` and `match_expression` and none
# for any loop kind, no `nir.Loop` is constructed anywhere in the
# file, and the loop reaches `expr()`'s catch-all `nir.Seq`, whose
# block handling routes the body's statements back through `expr()`
# (whose own `match_expression` case is a flat `nir.Seq`) rather than
# `stmt()` (whose case builds the `nir.Switch`). With flat regions
# `Dominates` degenerates to source order, so the bound sitting in
# the `b'"'` arm three arms away "dominates" the unguarded push and
# suppresses it.
#
# Re-measured on the real checkout against the current knowledge
# base. The graph shows the gap without a probe: all 111 call nodes
# inside `parse` sit at one flat region -- the bound `self.buf.len`
# at receiver.rs:280, the unguarded escaped-backslash push at :289
# and the `_` arm's bound at :297 are region siblings -- while
# functions whose `if`/`match` sit at statement position outside any
# loop get `if<n>.t` and `sw<n>.c` regions. Three `--cache off` runs
# per side, stable and identical at the parent and the fix: 7
# findings and 14 review flags, all memory (NullableDeref,
# IndexAccess) on protocol/fetch.rs, protocol/mod.rs and utf7.rs,
# none on receiver.rs, and `vyql match` on receiver.rs labels no
# source, no sink and no control at either revision. The Rust
# bindings shipped for the neighbouring unbounded-resource shapes do
# not reach this one: the streaming-decompression cap needs a
# decompress/inflate call, the OPC UA one needs the zero-sentinel
# limit literals, the NTS cookie one needs placeholder match arms
# plus cookie minting, and the `unbounded_next_await` review token
# needs `.next().await` -- this receiver's iterator is synchronous.
#
# The function-scoped alternative is measured not to discriminate. A
# probe binding in the shipped sibling style (`push` plus `next`, no
# min/clamp/truncate/resize in the function) reports
# `code.UnboundedResourceOperation` at receiver.rs:142 at BOTH
# revisions, 17 findings each, and carries 9 unrelated HIGH rows on
# files that merely grow a vector (parser/append.rs, list.rs,
# search.rs twice, sort.rs, status.rs, store.rs, protocol/mod.rs,
# utf7.rs); adding the sibling suppressor `take` silences
# receiver.rs at both revisions alike, because
# `std::mem::take(&mut self.request)` sits in the `b'\n'` arm. The
# only function-scope deltas the fix leaves are the count of `len`
# comparisons and the constant's name, so no function-scoped clause
# separates the arms. The ENGINE-GAPS.md entry for the Rust loop
# lowering stands; the binding and rule on the inconsistent-bound
# signal are the data half that follows it.
#
# Spec cve_rank1789 records the unbounded arm and the bounded arm,
# both inside a `while let` and both in statement position, all four
# asserting reject VYQL-DOS-042: when the loop lowering lands branch
# regions and an unbounded-accumulation binding ships, cases one and
# three must flip to expect.

test "rank1789: the escaped-backslash arm appends without the bound its siblings carry"
  lang rust
  file crates/imap-proto/src/receiver.rs
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  const QUOTED_ARG_MAX_LEN: usize = 4096;

  enum State {
      Argument { last_ch: u8 },
      ArgumentQuoted { escaped: bool },
  }

  struct Receiver {
      buf: Vec<u8>,
      state: State,
  }

  impl Receiver {
      fn error_reset(&mut self, _: &str) -> Error {
          self.buf.clear();
          Error::TooLong
      }

      pub fn parse(&mut self, bytes: &mut std::slice::Iter<'_, u8>) -> Result<(), Error> {
          #[allow(clippy::while_let_on_iterator)]
          while let Some(&ch) = bytes.next() {
              match self.state.clone() {
                  State::Argument { last_ch } => match ch {
                      b'"' if last_ch.is_ascii_whitespace() => {
                          self.state = State::ArgumentQuoted { escaped: false };
                      }
                      _ => {
                          if self.buf.len() < QUOTED_ARG_MAX_LEN {
                              self.buf.push(ch);
                              self.state = State::Argument { last_ch: ch };
                          } else {
                              return Err(self.error_reset("Quoted argument too long."));
                          }
                      }
                  },
                  State::ArgumentQuoted { escaped } => match ch {
                      b'"' => {
                          if !escaped {
                              self.buf.clear();
                              self.state = State::Argument { last_ch: b' ' };
                          } else if self.buf.len() < QUOTED_ARG_MAX_LEN {
                              self.buf.push(ch);
                              self.state = State::ArgumentQuoted { escaped: false };
                          } else {
                              return Err(self.error_reset("Quoted argument too long."));
                          }
                      }
                      b'\\' => {
                          if escaped {
                              self.buf.push(ch);
                          }
                          self.state = State::ArgumentQuoted { escaped: !escaped };
                      }
                      b'\n' => {
                          return Err(self.error_reset("Unterminated quoted argument."));
                      }
                      _ => {
                          if self.buf.len() < QUOTED_ARG_MAX_LEN {
                              if escaped {
                                  self.buf.push(b'\\');
                              }
                              self.buf.push(ch);
                              self.state = State::ArgumentQuoted { escaped: false };
                          } else {
                              return Err(self.error_reset("Quoted argument too long."));
                          }
                      }
                  },
              }
          }
          Ok(())
      }
  }

  enum Error {
      TooLong,
  }
  ```

